	Configure TETRA speech codec for a VMP[tx]
apifn	sm_vmptx_config_codec_tetra
params	sm_vmptx_codec_tetra_parms codecp
	The VMP[tx] to which to add the codec
field	tSMVMPtxId vmptx in
	The payload type identifer to use with this codec (see
	<a href="http://www.ietf.org/rfc/rfc3550.txt">IETF RFC 3550</a>
	section 13). Supplying a value of
	<code>-1</code> will remove any payload type configuration from the 
	codec preventing its use.
field	tSM_INT payload_type in
unstruct
	<p>
	There is not currently a standard packet encoding for wrapping 
	TETRA-encoded speech into RTP. This implementation creates RTP frames 
	that have standard RTP header followed by: ETSI two octet Payload header 
	(with bits for framing rate, frame number, information element control, 
	traffic type, contents control and payload) - the payload header follows 
	the format described in ETSI TS 100 392-3-8 V0.0.8 section 5.2.1 TETRA ISI 
	payload encoding. Two 18 octet tetra frames - each frame consisting of BFI 
	bit followed by 137 bits of tetra encoded data (holding 30ms of encoded 
	audio data according to traffic type 0 followed by 6 padding bits) - thus 
	this pair of frames conveys 60ms of audio.
	<p> 
	The tetra encoded data in the 18 octet tetra frames is always traffic type 
	0 - ACELP (ETS 300 395-2, 4.2.2.7) following MSB-LSB bit order.
	<p>
	This requires the module
modref	tetra
	to have been downloaded.
explain
	0
retval
