	mapping to
ref	payload_type.
	<p>
	It is possible to change the payload type mapping of a codec whilst a
	VMP[rx] remains valid by specifying a new payload type mapping for a
	given codec. This supersedes any previous mappings that were in effect
	for that codec.
	<p>
	If the call completes successfully, RTP packets arriving at the VMP[rx]
	with a payload type that matches a mapped type will be decoded using 
	the selected codec.
	<p>
	If a codec is given the payload type <code>-1</code> the codec is no
	longer valid for this RTP session, unless it is subsequently 
	reconfigured.
